  "description": "ASP.NET Core image middleware for EasyImageSharp: app.UseEasyImageSharp() resizes, crops, pads, re-orients and transcodes images on the fly from query commands (width, height, mode, anchor, format, quality, bgcolor, autoorient, sampler, rotate, flip), with HMAC-SHA256 signed URLs (key rotation, optional expiry), Accept-header WebP negotiation with Vary: Accept, ETag / Last-Modified / 304 handling, HEAD support, path-traversal-safe file sources, physical-disk and IDistributedCache output caches with atomic writes, output limits, a concurrency limiter that answers 503 when saturated, cancellation on client abort and a health check. Also includes the dependency-injection integration (services.AddEasyImageSharp(): decoder limits, pixel-buffer budget and parallelism from code or IConfiguration, validated on start, with ready-made DecoderOptions and ImageExecutionOptions), usable without the middleware. Fully managed; depends only on the ASP.NET Core shared framework.",
